Local fix to the installed tbetoolkits (TTK) one_hot golden function.

Without it TTK reports CST_GOLD: GOLDEN_FAILURE for every one_hot case, because
the golden raises before any comparison runs:

    Input must be scalar but has rank 1 for '{{node OneHot}} = OneHot[...]'
    with input shapes: [1,1,593,1,1], [1], [], []

TTK case lists carry scalar attrs as one-element lists ({'axis': -1,
'depth': [31]}), which is what the operator binding consumes, but TensorFlow's
gen_array_ops.one_hot requires a rank-0 depth. The NPU output was therefore
never compared against anything.

Applies to:
  ttk_test1/tbetoolkits/user_defined_modules/op/golden_funcs/transformation.py

This edit lives in an installed tbetoolkits tree, not in a repository, so it is
lost on reinstall or upgrade. It has no upstream home in either
compiler-team/tools (MR !21) or compiler-team/pyasc (MR !487).

Verified: CST_GOLD 100.0%, PRECISION_STATUS PASS on Ascend950PR_9599, CANN 9.1.0.
The operator invocation is unchanged; only the golden's local read is patched.

--- a/tbetoolkits/user_defined_modules/op/golden_funcs/transformation.py
+++ b/tbetoolkits/user_defined_modules/op/golden_funcs/transformation.py
@@ -888,6 +888,10 @@
     data2 = context.input_arrays[2]
     data_dtype = data1.dtype
     depth = context.other_runtime_params["depth"]
+    if isinstance(depth, (list, tuple)):
+        # TTK carries scalar attrs as one-element lists, which is what the
+        # operator binding consumes; TensorFlow's OneHot needs a rank-0 depth.
+        depth = depth[0]
     axis = context.other_compilation_params["axis"]
     on_value = tf.constant(data1, shape=(), dtype=data_dtype)
     off_value = tf.constant(data2, shape=(), dtype=data_dtype)
